{
	"name": "Sudden Growth",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/magic/nature/tree-spirit-black.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>You amplify springtime’s sudden burst of plants. As an action, you may touch the floor or slam a staff on the ground, causing a dense tangle of grasses and flowers to appear in a 30-foot radius centered on you. The effected area becomes difficult terrain, and creatures who first enter the area must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw versus your spell save DC or become slowed so long as they remain in the area of effect. The area persists so long as you can maintain concentration or until it is dispelled by magic such as @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-spells.Item.hms9kdl2qoqjjrs4]{Dispel Magic} or similar spells. You are unaffected by the difficult terrain caused by this spell, but it does not move with you. You may use this ability a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus per long rest.</p>",
